<title>INDIA: Indian soybean prices firm, processors buying.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean prices firm, processors buying.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices remained firm in central Indian markets on good demand from processing plants. Prices rose by 50-100 rupees per tonne in the markets of central India. Business volume was good and undertone was firm.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were also firm on limited supply against better demand in local market. Soyoil prices rose by 200 rupees per tonne today. Voume was good and the undertone was firm.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were also firm on limited selling. Soymeal yellow was $298-300 rupees per tonne FAS (Free Alongside Ship) in bulk for export. Rapeseed extraction was $117 per tonne FAS (Free Alongside Ship) in bulk for export and was 3,950-4,000 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on Rail) condition.</p>
